    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS). The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a `checkDigit` field to the Owner API response, computed as a single Luhn check digit over the digits of the owner's `customerCode`, following the existing pattern for derived fields in this Spring Boot app:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `checkDigit` property to the `Owner` schema (readOnly `int32`, 0\u20139), so the code generator produces the DTO field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a static `checkDigit(String customerCode)` method implementing the standard Luhn algorithm over the digits in the code (non-digits ignored), returning 0\u20139, or `null` when the code is `null`. This matches the `luhn(...)` reference the acceptance test uses.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Wired the new field via a `@Mapping` expression and a `formatCheckDigit(owner)` helper, consistent with the other derived fields (`membershipNumber`, `identityKey`, etc.).\n\nThe acceptance test `coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode` and the full suite pass.",
