    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change slots cleanly into an established pattern. `Owner` already hosts a family of pure, static derivation methods (`householdId`, `membershipNumber`, `membershipLevel`, `locality`, `contactPreference`, `identityKey`), and `OwnerMapper` has a matching `format*` default method for each that handles the null-owner case and delegates to the model. The new `Owner.checkDigit(String)` and `OwnerMapper.formatCheckDigit(Owner)` mirror this split exactly:\n\n- Computation logic lives in the model (`Owner`), parameterized on just `customerCode`, consistent with its siblings \u2014 the right unit for deterministic derivation.\n- The mapper method does only the null guard + field extraction + delegation, like every neighboring `format*` method, and is placed adjacent to `formatIdentityKey`.\n- The `@Mapping` annotation and OpenAPI schema entry follow the surrounding entries' ordering and style.\n\nNo duplication, no catch-all accretion, nothing miscategorized. A maintainer of this codebase would find it entirely natural.",
